    "letter": "a",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1963-p33.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The given line is \\(3x-4y+24=0.\\) A parallel line \\(y=\\frac{3x}{4}+b\\) is \\(3x-4y+4b=0,\\) so the distance is \\(\\frac{|24-4b|}{5}.\\) Setting this equal to \\(4\\) gives \\(|6-b|=5,\\) hence \\(b=1\\) or \\(11.\\) Choice A is possible.\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Write parallel lines as \\(3x-4y+c=0\\)",
        "The distance equals the absolute difference of constants divided by \\(5\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
